    <!--
      Franchise screen row: a portrait poster with the list-status button 1dp under it.

      The poster is a fixed width rather than a share of the row, and the synopsis takes
      whatever is left. That is the whole sizing decision: a weighted split would grow the
      poster with the screen until on a tablet it was most of the width and the prose it is
      supposed to sit beside had nothing to sit in. Fixed, it stays a poster at every size,
      and the column that grows with the screen is the one carrying the text.

      2:3, the usual poster proportion, so the picture is not stretched. The height comes
      from that ratio in the layout rather than from a second number here, because two
      numbers kept in step by hand is a number that will drift.
    -->
    <dimen name="franchise_poster_width">136dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_row_margin">24dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_row_gap">3dp</dimen>
    <!--
      The clear band between one card column and the next, and the run the connector lives in.

      This is not spacing for its own sake: the line leaves card N's foot and arrives at card
      N+1's head across exactly this band, and the chevron that points into the next card is
      about 12dp tall. At 12dp the band was the same height as the arrow, so the arrow filled it
      edge to edge and there was no air anywhere in it. 20dp leaves the arrow room to sit inside
      the gap rather than touching the cards on either side of it.
    -->
    <dimen name="franchise_row_bottom_margin">20dp</dimen>
    <!-- 1dp under the poster, before the list-status button. -->
    <dimen name="franchise_list_status_top">1dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_list_status_height">30dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_info_size">30dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_rating_margin">8dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_card_corner">20dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_synopsis_gap">6dp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_title_size">14sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_synopsis_size">12sp</dimen>
    <!--
      The year, over the artwork at the poster's foot.

      Bigger than the other poster marks on purpose. It is the one piece of metadata the row
      does not say anywhere else: the title beside the poster names the entry, and the entry's
      own screen carries the format and the runtime, but the year appears nowhere except here,
      and at 11sp it sat under the info button as a caption rather than as a date you could read
      from across a room. 13sp is enough to hold its own against the 10sp rating without starting
      to compete with the poster it is printed on.
    -->
    <dimen name="franchise_year_size">13sp</dimen>
    <dimen name="franchise_meta_size">10sp</dimen>

    <!--
      How much of the poster's foot the gradient covers, measured up from the bottom edge.

      Tall enough to sit behind the info button, the year and their padding, plus a little run
      in above them so the ramp starts somewhere rather than arriving abruptly. Not a fraction
      of the poster's height: the two marks are a fixed dp tall whatever the poster is, so a
      percentage would make the ramp's reach depend on the screen size for no gain.
    -->
    <dimen name="franchise_poster_gradient_height">76dp</dimen>
</resources>